The sentiment analysis provides no directional conviction, with near-zero readings across news and social sentiment. The recent news appears generic and contradictory, offering no Bitcoin-specific catalysts. Most concerning is that this setup fails our minimum confidence threshold of 60% and lacks a clear edge despite reasonable liquidity. With Bitcoin needing only a small push to hit $100K, the 53% implied probability appears rationally priced given current market conditions.

