The technical indicators show oversold conditions (RSI at 25) and strong bearish momentum (-15% rate of change), suggesting the market has overreacted negatively to recent information. This oversold condition, combined with spiking volume, indicates potential capitulation selling that often precedes reversals. While sentiment remains neutral, the lack of strong negative sentiment despite the bearish price action suggests the selloff may be more technical than fundamental.

